            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of inflammatory, neuropathic and sympathetically maintained pain in a patient with Sjögren's syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>205-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of Sjögren's syndrome with a painful peripheral neuropathy where pain control required both anti-inflammatory and sympatholytic treatments. This case suggests that the pain in some inflammatory disorders with nerve injury may have a component mediated by an alpha adrenergic receptor.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
